WEBVTT

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.820
You're looking pretty slick, huh?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.070
What the heck's with you, all dressed up nice?

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.500
This is the stuff Isamu used to wear.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.270
It was all special-made for him last year.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.070
They're good clothes, but they're already too small for me.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.410
So they're hand-me-downs.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.430
He was looking too shabby.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.270
When he's got a date no less.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.180
So that's it. It's today, huh?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.820
Good morning.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.600
Good morning...

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.270
Are you going?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.140
Thank you so much for this today.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:44.540
No, it's fine, but don't forget your curfew.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.030
Be sure you're home by dinnertime.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.400
Yes, Ma'am. Well, I'll be going now.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.180
It really is a date.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.160
What?

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.570
Nothing.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.800
I'm going out as well just after noon, so...

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.170
Look after things for me, please.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.140
I know your hands right away, Tatsuya.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:50.200
Warm, a little damp... Gentle hands, like a girl's.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.710
It's been a while.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.680
Uh-huh.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.850
Have you been well?

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:55.810
Uh-huh.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:02.990
I've wanted to see you.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:03.960
Uh-huh.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:06.690
Nothing but "uh-huh, uh-huh"?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:07.660
Uh-huh...

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.100
Have you grown again?

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.130
I'm taller than you by now.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.270
Here's a ticket.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:30.250
It's an open pass for everything, so let's go all out to have fun in the time we've got.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.480
Uh-huh!

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.030
A piano recycling shop?

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.090
That's right.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.190
What kind of work are you doing there?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.030
Taking rust off the pedals, cleaning the insides of pianos...

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.160
I'm still just an apprentice.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.340
What about tuning?

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:57.410
I did it once, just to try it, but it was no good.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.930
Afterwards, when someone corrected it for me, it was completely different.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.880
Not just the pitch, but the tone and the resonance too.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.010
So much so, I almost wondered if it was really the same piano.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.420
How about boyfriends and stuff?

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:15.090
I have some.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.720
You do...

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.670
Pianos, the pianos are my boyfriends now.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.040
Oh, come on, that was true even up until now, wasn't it?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.940
It'll be that way from now on too.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.270
How about you, Tatsuya?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.240
What about that girl? You're always together, right?

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.270
No way... She's not my type, and she's weird too.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.990
Ow! What was that for?!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.960
It's your fault for being in such a daze!

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.470
Hey...

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.470
I want you to give me some Dynamis.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.040
I'd rather not. You're only going to use it to fool around, aren't you?

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.880
It's only when the Countess goes out that we can do stuff like that, right?

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.280
Come on, I said come on.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.810
You're a pest.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.520
Thanks.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.960
What are you studying?

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.240
You're good at that, better than Toru.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.300
Madoka's more to your liking now, right?

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.580
What are you talking about?

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.210
That little boy with his sister complex?

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.210
Ah-choo!

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.910
Take care of yourself.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:11.170
Orga... Organ, organism, organization, organon...

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.150
Internal organ...

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:20.440
I see, that woman was at Heaven's Gate. That makes sense.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:29.060
After all, it was clear when we first met her that the woman knew us.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.170
And her eyes... When she looked at you, she seemed to be overlaying Dad's image onto you.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.350
You didn't notice?

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.030
No...

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.720
You're so dense.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.560
Tatsuya, little by little you've come to look just like Dad.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.040
This piece...

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.230
It's from "The Merry Widow."

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.340
That woman apparently knows Mom too.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.250
She was talking about her at one point:

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.250
"Slovenly, filthy, unsightly and alcohol-sodden," she said.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.300
Certainly right on the mark.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.530
A long time ago, she wasn't like that, right?

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.090
What kind of a mother was she?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.110
Attractive...

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.870
Attractive?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.900
She had a good figure and she always seemed so dashing,

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.200
...always cheerful.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.410
Why did she end up like...

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.280
All I can say is that, when it came down to it, she was weak as a person.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.420
It's a rare occasion that we're seeing each other, so let's stop with this kind of talk.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:15.260
It's the Turangalila!

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:22.270
I saw it up close when I went to the Settlement.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.710
It was an amazing facility.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:30.670
The October Project... They say if it succeeds, it'll bring back the world as it was before Twin X.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.350
But those people...

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:38.210
They'll commit more acts of terrorism.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.660
It'll be fine, because we're here.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.700
We will protect the Turangalila. You'll see.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.700
With the bright future everybody has been anxiously awaiting finally about to begin...

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.240
I wonder about that.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.680
I think it would be good if the mirror were gone too.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.980
But still, isn't that a bit presumptuous?

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.480
To assume the sky's restoration will make for a bright future?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.620
Even if the Sheltering Sky vanishes,

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.990
...only a certain set of people will benefit from it.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.960
I think it's something that might not have much to do with us.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:23.790
I may not be much, but I still know just a little more about the world than you, Tatsuya.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.310
Kiyoko, you know...

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.830
What?

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:32.400
Little by little, you've gotten to be like Mom.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.650
Doing nothing but complaining all the time...

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:40.080
Last time you said that woman...

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.050
Now, this time I'm like Mom?!

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.320
Kiyoko! Wait a minute!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.360
Pardon me!

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.780
What's up with that, Kiyoko?

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:27.020
Couldn't you have easily found me using Dynamis?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.350
Are you gonna be okay? With that level of skill...

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.160
You weren't watching me from a distance this whole time, were you?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:39.070
I can tell right away where you are, Tatsuya.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:45.880
That's mean...

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:49.910
You're mean!

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:57.580
There, there. Your big sister was in the wrong.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.590
You're not mad about what I said earlier?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.570
I'm more of an adult than before.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.060
It's just that you were saying such naïve things,

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.960
...I started to want to give you a hard time.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.310
You're a horrible sister.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.370
I'm sorry. I feel bad about what I said too.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:28.780
You're certainly right. It's just like you said, Tatsuya.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.790
Don't ever do anything like this again, okay?

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:37.460
I know.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.670
I didn't think it was gonna rain or anything.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.690
It's clear off in the distance. It'll stop soon.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.830
I somehow get the feeling I'm always being hounded by rain.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.310
It's because you're a rain man, Tatsuya.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.400
No I'm not. You're a rain woman!

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.680
Wasn't that day the same?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.150
That piano... I wonder if it's getting wet right now?

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:10.350
You found that tuning fork there, didn't you?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.740
I've got it with me even now.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.140
Look!

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.740
Still serving as a good-luck charm?

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.210
Now it's a tool of the trade.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.780
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.720
This is where you work?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:41.120
Yeah, I have to work now, because one's being brought in tonight.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.790
I already can't see your face, Tatsuya.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.130
Thanks for walking me here.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.030
Yeah, well...

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:05.180
Bye-bye.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:13.570
That outfit must be nice and cool in the summertime, yes?

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:15.820
How long have you known?

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.690
For a long time.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:22.090
I hear the piano shop you managed to get into went out of business right away.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:26.760
Then after losing your means of livelihood, you took another job here, is that it?

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:32.840
When you left the hotel, I marveled at what half-baked things you were saying,

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.810
...but now it looks as though I'll find it possible to like you.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.980
Are you going to tell my brother?

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:42.510
What would doing something like that accomplish?

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:45.740
All I care about is that you send me what I'm owed every month.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.320
Anyway, it's for the best if I don't say anything.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.810
It would be a bit too much stimulation for a boy in puberty.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:04.640
Did you come today to make fun of me?

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:06.800
I'm afraid I don't have that much leisure time.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.270
There's a little something I want to ask about.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:16.740
Regarding the secret of Tatsuya's birth.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.750
About how he's not really the child of your father, Terumichi Madoka, for instance.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.990
You should know better than anyone that Tatsuya looks just like my father, right?

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.300
Yes, truly, like two peas in a pod.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.460
So much so, that one might say there's too much resemblance.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:43.710
I wonder why your mother had Tatsuya, even though it meant taking on a considerable debt?

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.630
Is there a connection between Tatsuya and the debt?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.500
Most of the obligation that you're now bearing...

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:54.880
...was something incurred a year before that boy was born.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.320
You know that, correct?

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.130
There's no way the expenses for childbirth could have been that much.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:05.290
They could have been, if she'd given birth to an exceptional child.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:11.630
The evidence of that is that he can use Dynamis, unlike you.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.880
If it had been an ordinary pregnancy,

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.150
...there should also have been the option of getting rid of it.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:25.640
Right after Twin X, it was sheer madness, her having the child of the terrorist.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:32.050
From the very beginning, Mom never believed that Dad did it.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:38.590
That's why she said to me, "You and this child have to clear your father's reputation."

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.970
I'm sure that's what she said.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.630
Your mother did?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.970
"Because the child that will be born is a boy,"

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.200
"...and he'll understand your father better than anyone," she said.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.780
I see.

00:18:56.310 --> 00:19:00.250
So that's how it was? That's all I need to know.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.690
Well then, it's about time for me to get back,

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.990
...though it's regrettable that I can't see your performance.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.860
"That's how it was?" What does that mean?

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:14.830
Thank you for an interesting chat.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:17.100
I'm grateful for the good service.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.070
I'm home.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.340
Welcome back.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.970
How was your date?

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.840
All right...

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:33.980
I got this.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.920
Huh? For me?

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.510
Because you wanted it.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:45.330
I'm so glad you remembered then.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.930
They had the exact one, so...

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.060
Thanks. Madoka, you're sweet.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:52.500
Ah-choo!

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:53.470
Do you have a cold?

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:53.700
It's nothing. Ah-choo!
Do you have a cold?

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.730
It's nothing. Ah-choo!

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:03.480
Welcome home, my lady.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:04.710
I'm back.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.620
Well? Did you enjoy yourself?

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:08.390
Yes, Ma'am.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:12.180
Please tell me all about it at dinnertime.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:13.350
Yes, Ma'am.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:20.330
My lady, a messenger from the Yuki household brought this earlier.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:26.470
Did that old gentleman pass away?

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:30.270
No, my lady, it is an invitation to a living funeral.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:31.900
A living funeral?

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:37.650
The gentleman says he would like to say farewell to those persons who did so much for him while he is still alive.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:40.810
He says he would like, by all means, to request your presence, my lady.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:49.260
I see. Please inform him that I would be delighted to attend, and that the children will be attending with me.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.560
As you wish, my lady.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:54.990
And might something have happened, my lady?

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.030
I ask because you're rather, shall I say...

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:01.500
...in higher spirits, than before you left.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.800
No, nothing in particular.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.840
I'm suppose I'm what you'd call the Merry Widow.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:13.450
Welcome home.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:14.510
I'm back.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:16.650
If I may...

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:18.020
What is it?

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.790
Won't you let us in on some things, sometime soon?

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:25.490
Things like what Orga refers to, and what Dynamis is.

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:30.800
As to that, I think some of the things you want to know...

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:35.170
...might become clear on the occasion of this memorial service.

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:28.290
An innocent smile, knowing no corruption...

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:30.220
What sort of person is Mr. Yuki?

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:32.790
Everything around her is filled to overflowing with happiness,

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:34.090
...blessing that beauty.

00:23:34.090 --> 00:23:37.460
He's the man who had Heaven's Gate built too, right?

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:38.600
That was a tremendous sense of malice.

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:40.730
If I like her, it's the young Hiroko I like.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:42.470
A monster from the previous century, huh?

00:23:42.470 --> 00:23:43.970
It's not the sour one.

00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:46.340
We thought it was about time we knew about ourselves.

00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:47.000
Pretty, huh?

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:48.640
She just evades all our questions.

00:23:48.640 --> 00:23:50.440
They fled that time...

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:52.540
A stronghold of evil where a monster dwells, huh?

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.670
If you don't watch it, you'll turn into a pig!
